  "limitations": [
    "Flower and Opacus are not used: torch/flwr/opacus are not installable in this environment (CUDA wheel size, fastapi pin conflict). The regimes and the RDP accountant are implemented directly in numpy/scipy and are measured, not quoted.",
    "n=8 participants from one public exercise dataset; participant bootstrap CIs are wide and cannot support a clinical or spaceflight claim.",
    "IMPORTANT: every regime lands close to the training-mean baseline. The frozen M6 run found the same thing (ridge A4 32.22 bpm vs the 24.18 bpm mean baseline), so these 41 features do not generalise across participants. The near-zero measured DP cost is a consequence of no regime learning much, NOT evidence that strong privacy is free here.",
    "the linear model is deliberately simple so all four regimes share one step budget; this is a training-regime comparison, not a state-of-the-art HR model.",
    "DP noise is applied per client per step with a fixed denominator; epsilon is composed over rounds x local_steps for the smallest client (worst case)."
  ],
  "model": "linear least squares trained by minibatch SGD (identical model and step budget in all four regimes, so the comparison isolates the training regime)",
  "preprocessing": "features z-scored and target standardised using TRAIN-participant statistics only, per fold; predictions converted back to bpm before scoring. The DP clip norm C=1.0 therefore acts on a comparable scale in every fold. These statistics are not DP-protected.",
